            <ArticleTitle>Successful surgical treatment for a thrombus straddling a patent foramen ovale: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>138</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1186/1749-8090-8-138</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Paradoxical embolism (PDE) occurs after embolic material passes from the venous to the arterial circulation through a right-to-left shunt, which is frequently a patent foramen ovale (PFO). We describe the case of a patient with deep venous thrombosis and an intracardiac thrombus straddling a PFO and who was successfully treated with an emergency surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
